      "text": "To determine the fraction of the items on the menu that I can eat, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the total number of dishes on the menu.**\n   - We are given that one fifth of the menu consists of meatless dishes. Since there are four meatless dishes that are not made with gluten, this means the total number of meatless dishes (including those made with gluten) is:\n     \\[\n     4 \\text{ (meatless dishes without gluten)} + 3 \\text{ (meatless dishes made with gluten)} = 7 \\text{ (total meatless dishes)}\n     \\]\n   - Since this is one fifth of the total menu, we can find the total number of dishes on the menu by multiplying both sides of the equation by 5:\n     \\[\n     7 \\times 5 = 35 \\text{ (total dishes on the menu)}\n     \\]\n\n2. **Determine the number of dishes I can eat.**\n   - I can only eat the meatless dishes that do not contain gluten. From the problem, we know that:\n     - There are initially 7 meatless dishes.\n     - Out of these, 3 are made with gluten, so the number of meatless dishes that do not contain gluten is:\n       \\[\n       7 - 3 = 4\n       \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the fraction of the menu that I can eat.**\n   - The fraction of the total menu that I can eat is the number of dishes I can eat divided by the total number of dishes on the menu:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{4}{35}\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the fraction of the items on the menu that I can eat is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{4}{35}}\\).",
